<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Rhandeia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">62</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-parthian-war-of-58-63">Roman–Parthian War of 58–63</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Rhandeia was fought in 62 CE in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> during the war between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthia">Parthia</a> over the Armenian throne. A Roman army under Lucius Caesennius Paetus was besieged by the Parthian king Vologases I at Rhandeia and forced to accept humiliating terms. The settlement that followed in 63 let the Parthian prince Tiridates rule Armenia but receive his crown from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a> in Rome.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-rhandeia.jpg" alt="Battle of Rhandeia" width="320" height="194" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cplakidas · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman-Parthian_War_61-63.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
